      "problem": "$\\frac{(-5)^{7}\\cdot (-5)^{5}}{(-5)^{8}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the numerator using the product rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(-5)^{7}\\cdot (-5)^{5}}{(-5)^{8}}=\\frac{(-5)^{7+5}}{(-5)^{8}}=\\frac{(-5)^{12}}{(-5)^{8}}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the quotient rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(-5)^{12}}{(-5)^{8}}=(-5)^{12-8}=(-5)^{4}\n$$",
